on-arrival: f_ev_last = time

= El que no puede caminar

He took it through the hip two days ago and the column has been carrying him since, four men at a time on a litter, at a third of its normal speed, with the ring closing. The médico — if you have one — says he lives if he stops moving and dies if he does not. The map says the column dies if it stops moving. This is the arithmetic Che wrote about and could not solve either, and it is now sitting by the fire looking at you with complete understanding.

- @her_cargar: Carry him. The column moves at his speed and takes whatever comes. *(major risk; the band's soul)*
- @her_esconder: Leave him in a village with people who will hide and nurse him. *(faster; you are trusting a whole hamlet with a man's life and your security)*
- @her_dejar: Leave him with a weapon and a canteen where he chose to be left. *(the column survives; everyone knows what happened)*

@her_cargar
on-arrival: {! Q.f_cerco+=20; if(Q.f_cerco>100){Q.f_cerco=100;} Q.f_moral+=12; Q.f_comida-=6; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)+3; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+2; if(Math.random()*100 < (Q.f_cerco||0)*0.5){ Q.f_hombres-=3; Q.f_bajas+=3; Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+2; } !}

You carry him, and the column crawls, and the ring draws in around the four men on the litter and the twenty walking beside them at half speed. [? if f_cerco >= 80 : They catch the tail of the column in a draw and it costs you three more to get everyone out, which is precisely the arithmetic the manual warned about. ?] He lives. And every fighter in the band now knows, with certainty rather than hope, that they will not be left — which is worth more than a road, and which you have just paid for at the going rate.

- @root: Continuar.

@her_esconder
on-arrival: {! Q.f_cerco-=6; if(Q.f_cerco<0){Q.f_cerco=0;} var _rr=Math.random()*100; if(_rr < 30 + (Q.apoyo_popular||0)*0.5){ Q.f_moral+=5; var _h=Math.max(0,(Q.apoyo_techo||55)-(Q.apoyo_popular||0)); Q.apoyo_popular+=Math.min(5,_h*0.3); } else { Q.f_hombres-=1; Q.f_bajas+=1; Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+1; Q.apoyo_popular-=6; Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+5; } !}

You leave him under a floor in a hamlet with a family who agree instantly, the way people here always agree, and the column moves on at speed. [? if apoyo_popular >= 50 : Six weeks later he walks back into camp with a limp and a great deal to say about the woman who nursed him. The water held. ?][? if apoyo_popular < 50 : Three weeks later the army searches that hamlet on a tip and finds him, and afterwards the family is gone too. You did not have enough water to float that decision, and other people paid for the difference. ?]

- @root: Continuar.

@her_dejar
on-arrival: {! Q.brutalidad=(Q.brutalidad||0)+1; Q.f_cerco-=14; if(Q.f_cerco<0){Q.f_cerco=0;} Q.f_moral-=16; Q.disciplina=(Q.disciplina||65)-4; Q.f_hombres-=1; Q.memorial=(Q.memorial||0)+1; Q.paranoia=(Q.paranoia||8)+6; !}

He says he understands and he asks for the pistol, and the column marches away at full speed and gets clear, which was the correct military decision and is the one nobody will ever discuss again. It is also the sentence every man in the band now silently completes about himself. Morale is not a number after a morning like that; it is the specific weight of knowing what the movement does when you cannot walk.

- @root: Continuar.
